{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76490-hunter-the-reckoning-help-me-pick-a-world-locale","id":76490,"title":"[Hunter:The Reckoning] Help me pick a world locale","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-21T12:30:07-08:00","id":76490,"title":"[Hunter:The Reckoning] Help me pick a world locale","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">So I've GM'd Hunter: The Reckoning for awhile, setting the games in places that were easy for my players to grasp (North America, Canada, UK). After 9-11 though, I always had a tough time in my mind holding together the suspension of disbelief. While gun crime is still rampant in the US, I feel like a group of people organizing and arming themselves would be hounded by the FBI, ATF, and everyone else. Likewise, I just want to take the players out of their comfort zone and throw them at some new situations. I decided to jump out and run a game in some interesting international locations. Problem is, I can't decide which one (they all seem so great!). </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1. Brazil: Setting a game in Rio would provide for a unique experience while not being too &quot;foreign&quot; to the players. Between the favelas, drug dealers, and government corruption - I'm sure I could spin an interesting tale. However I somehow feel that Brazil might not be as target rich environment as my other locales. I get the impression that werewolves probably aren't present, and I don't even want to delve into the other were-creatures (we will not be fighting Street Sharks.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2. Mexico: Again, a setting that my players are probably somewhat more familiar with. I have the opportunity to create some great stories ripped straight form the headlines with all the cartel nonsense going on. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">3. Syria: In the midst of a civil war, this could provide an interesting look into the unfamiliar. Likewise the middle east have a plethora of interesting monsters (Followers of the Set, Assamites, Mummies). The only problems are that it's hard to research how life is for a regular person in the midst of the turmoil. It might be to much of a task to have the players not get involved (or at least overshadowed) by the civil war. A good alternative might be Lebanon. Which still has a history of war, but is now trying to pick up the pieces from decades of conflict. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">4. Thailand: Bangkok would be a beautiful city to run a game in. Throw in some Kindred of the East in the mix of traditional monsters and it might be a good romp. Indonesia could be a good alternative too. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">5. South Africa: Jo-burg is such a crazy mix of culture, history, and urban sprawl amidst a different landscape. We could touch on the crime, relics of apartheid, and the characters would probably be great. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">6.Other: please detail.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2296-icemaster109","name":"icemaster109","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T13:18:17-08:00","id":76522,"title":"","content":"South Africa would be cool, as would Rio. Though to be honest, I'm not sure I agree with your assessment of a post 9-11 Hunter group in the U.S. and the difficulty they would have. I'd argue it's no more difficult now, than it was then, to organize and arm a group. They are still gangs and other organizations all across the U.S. that the FBI/CIA/DEA, etc. have difficulty touching. Organizations on a much larger scale than the Hunter groups I've played with. Small Hunter groups would make it easier, in my opinion. And sure, traveling might be more difficult, but there are ways around that, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T14:24:06-08:00","id":76577,"title":"","content":"First, I agree with DoL - the various Alphabet Soup agencies are a part of life and really always have been. Now they just have a few more things they can throw at you <i>if</i> they catch you and feel like it - but really, it's just a few more things, and not nearly as bad as, say, mass murder, which your average hunter is likely to &quot;commit&quot; when s/he &quot;kills&quot; a group of zombies.<br /> <br /> Second, as far as locations go outside the typical First World settings, each of your suggestions has something going for it and something agin' it. For example, I have absolutely no doubt that there are in fact <i>tons</i> of shifters in Rio - along with vampires, of course (and stranger things). Mexico, at least near the capital, seems like a bad idea for a variety of reasons (Sabbat packs not the least of them), but set it in, say, Cozumel or whatnot? You get Sabbat packs, visiting kindred, some shifters, ghosts, whatever.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Syria, though the civil war may overwhelm your story if you're not careful. An alternative to that (and Lebanon) is something like Jordan. If you go this route, make sure you make use of <i>Holy War</i>. I don't really know enough about Bangkok to speak, but I do know it's gotten a lot &quot;cleaner&quot; in the last few decades (which is sorta like saying my cat box is &quot;cleaner&quot; after I empty it, granted). That said, this is the WoD, so that may not have happened.<br /> <br /> South Africa is an interesting choice, too. If you have KotEK it might be entertaining to throw something like that in.<br /> <br /> Other places? The Ukraine is a bit of a disaster area ATM, so there's that. I suspect a better bet might be, say, Moscow or somewhere else in Russia (who can then visit Ukraine). Australia has some pretty massive benefits, among them the fact that it's a melting pot of all the various other supernaturals out there - and where else can you leave your hunters in the Outback? Japan - Tokyo specifically - makes a fascinating place. The main drawback to that or anywhere in China is then you pretty much have to use KotE critters, and not everyone likes to do that. But Tokyo offers Aokigahara Forest... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:19:11-08:00","id":76628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>icemaster109</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76490-hunter-the-reckoning-help-me-pick-a-world-locale#post76490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">1. Brazil: Setting a game in Rio would provide for a unique experience while not being too &quot;foreign&quot; to the players. Between the favelas, drug dealers, and government corruption - I'm sure I could spin an interesting tale. However I somehow feel that Brazil might not be as target rich environment as my other locales. I get the impression that werewolves probably aren't present, and I don't even want to delve into the other were-creatures (we will not be fighting Street Sharks.)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">2. Mexico: Again, a setting that my players are probably somewhat more familiar with. I have the opportunity to create some great stories ripped straight form the headlines with all the cartel nonsense going on. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>On Brazil/Mexico:</b></u> The most you would encounter with other shapeshifters are: Balam (Jaguars), Ratkin (Rats), Mokole (Crocodiles that can turn into Dinosaurs), Corax (Ravens/Crows), Ananasi (Spiders), and Garou (Werewolves). The only way to encounter Rokea (Sharks) is being near the coast or ocean in pretty much any location. There is one Rokea from the Rokea breed book that swims in the Amazon rivers, but because he is far away from the ocean: He's stuck in Shark Man form and cannot change any more. The Garou come in numbers to fight the Amazon war waged against what Pentex controlled companies are doing down there.<br /> There was also a recent Smithsonian Magazine article (<a href=\"http://www.smithsonianmag.com/science-nature/why-do-environmentalists-keep-getting-killed-around-world-180949446/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood in the Jungle by Scott Wallace</a>) about the brutal slayings of local environmentalists in the area.<br /> <br /> Mexico also has a lot of Black Spiral Dancers, besides Bone Gnawer Garou, Ratkin, and the Balam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T15:57:55-08:00","id":76667,"title":"","content":"I won's speak to Africa and Thailand.<br /> <br /> Rio: Look up a few things: Candombl\u00e9, Confederados, and did you know that almost 30% of the people of Guyana are Hindu by faith. Jaguar and Mokol\u00e9 would be your primary shifters in the region. Changelings may have or be a part of the Orisha system, or completely different. The Inca used to cross into Brazil to practice genocide against the headhunting tribes (who would shrink the heads down using heat and sand) as they feared these people ate or used the souls of such dead. Also, remember many Nazis are rumored to have fled there - perhaps Progenitor experiments on genetic purity continue today. I read once where the Confederados used to meat in Rio for a grand ball to celebrate their origens by wearing the uniforms and dresses of their Confederate States of American ancestors. A wild Confederado gala could be a wonderful starting point.<br /> <br /> Instead of Syria, consider Mumbai, India or Kurdistan. I pick these because both have Zarthoshti either in them or as a heritage. In Zartoshti belief hunting Khrafstra (beasts) is a meritorious act. Khrafstra have the following characteristics: 1) they harm humans, livestock, and grain, 2) they are ugly and abominable, 3) they live in darkness, 4) they pollute creation and the sacred elements. If you go with the Kurds, then consider David Rohl's &quot;From Eden to Exile&quot; where he suggests they were one of the first peoples to be subjected to total war by a corrupt Sumerian empire seeking to take holy rocks from their lands. Further, Zoroastrianism can provide you with a wealth of demonic forces, servants of Angra Mainyu as adversaries for your group. We have not even considered the Greek influences from the empire of Alexander the Accursed (Great) into Persia, the origens of the Baali, Ahl-i-Batin, Assamites, etc. Further, Kurdistan is an unrecognized area with the largest disenfranchised ethnic group in the world - with territory claimed in Syria, Turkey, Iraq, and Iran. Also read up on the Yezidi - who hold that the angel did not rebel against God and is the highest of the 7 archangels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T17:18:17-08:00","id":76715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Hyena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76490-hunter-the-reckoning-help-me-pick-a-world-locale?p=76628#post76628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <u><b>On Brazil/Mexico:</b></u> The most you would encounter with other shapeshifters are: Balam (Jaguars), Ratkin (Rats), Mokole (<b>Crocodiles that can turn into Dinosaurs</b>), Corax (Ravens/Crows), Ananasi (Spiders), and Garou (Werewolves). The only way to encounter Rokea (Sharks) is being near the coast or ocean in pretty much any location. There is one Rokea from the Rokea breed book that swims in the Amazon rivers, but because he is far away from the ocean: He's stuck in Shark Man form and cannot change any more. The Garou come in numbers to fight the Amazon war waged against what Pentex controlled companies are doing down there.<br /> There was also a recent Smithsonian Magazine article (<a href=\"http://www.smithsonianmag.com/science-nature/why-do-environmentalists-keep-getting-killed-around-world-180949446/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood in the Jungle by Scott Wallace</a>) about the brutal slayings of local environmentalists in the area.<br /> <br /> Mexico also has a lot of Black Spiral Dancers, besides Bone Gnawer Garou, Ratkin, and the Balam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caimans (technically more like alligators). Crocs would be found in a theoretical population of Middle Dragons born from a large population of Asian immigrants to South America, but not among Amazon's Mokole-mbembe.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T18:30:08-08:00","id":76760,"title":"","content":"I find the idea of a game set in the Carribean to be an interesting idea. Not tied to any one locale, though perhaps a nomadic group of hunters, island hopping to avoid the heat from both the monsters and the governments. You could play around with and experience many different and fascinating cultures and locales; the Carribean is a real melting pot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T21:07:01-08:00","id":76842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/76490-hunter-the-reckoning-help-me-pick-a-world-locale?p=76715#post76715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Caimans (technically more like alligators). Crocs would be found in a theoretical population of Middle Dragons born from a large population of Asian immigrants to South America, but not among Amazon's Mokole-mbembe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for catching the mistake, Saur. Was just remembering off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-21T22:03:02-08:00","id":76870,"title":"","content":"Wow, you guys are actually making the choice <b>harder </b>with so many good ideas. Now in addition to my choices, I'm considering Mumbai, India, Kurdistan, and the Caribbean Isles. All excellent ideas. Keep the good ideas coming. However I need to start eliminating them (or maybe putting them on a backburner for later use).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2296-icemaster109","name":"icemaster109","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}